  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender and HIV&amp;AIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcomes:
1.	15 local community initiatives actively working to change gender power relations and running stigma-free HIV and AIDS initiatives in at least 6 local township and semi-rural communities in the Umgungundlovu District. 
2.	All PACSA programmes fully mainstreamed HIV and Gender into their work and have a functioning organisational structure, engaging effectively on gender and HIV-related issues and policies with various stakeholders, as relevant to them.
3. Community Partner organizations have formed significant links with other organizations or movement engaged in similar struggles at local, national and regional levels
4. The programme has capacity to implement its work and contributes to that of its community partners and other civil society formations.
Pietermaritzburg Agency for Christian Social Awareness (PACSA) and community partners  in the Umgungundlovu District have been implementing a programme geared towards engaging meaningfully participation in Gender and HIV-related issues and policies for the promotion of gender equality, reduction in gender based violence, and improved health. The projected outcomes include at least 15 local community initiatives will be actively working to change gender power relations and running stigma-free HIV and AIDS initiatives in at least 6 local township and semi-rural communities in the Umgungundlovu District. Internally, PACSA intends to mainstream HIV and Gender into their work. PACSA is working with community based groups and churches as partners in conceptualisation and implementation. Over the next 3 years, the programme will accompany at least 15 poor and marginalised community groups, reaching over 5000 men, women and youth in total annually.</narrative>
  </description>
